# Times are UTC. The first two replace vercel.json's crons, same schedule.
# cron-job.org keeps its own jobs; they call the public domain as before.
0 6 * * * /ops/cron-call.sh /api/admin/settle
30 10 * * * /ops/cron-call.sh /api/admin/curate-accumulators
# Nightly backup at 02:30 UTC (03:30 Lagos), the quietest hour.
30 2 * * * /ops/backup.sh

# Controlled early-fixture rollout: these routes are opt-in inside the app.
# Defaults are OFF, so scheduling alone cannot create or publish new tips.
# The work is internal to the VPS and uses the existing CRON_SECRET; do NOT
# duplicate the same endpoints in cron-job.org.
3,33 * * * * /ops/cron-call.sh /api/admin/generate/early-discover?batch=4
6,36 * * * * /ops/cron-call.sh /api/admin/generate/early-odds?limit=4
# early-run shares the "generation-run" lease (6-minute TTL, worker.ts) with
# ordinary (10,25,40,55), VIP/Premium (5,20,35,50) and European (15,45)
# generation, all on cron-job.org in Lagos time (= UTC+1, so the minutes are
# identical). At :09/:39 an early run still awaiting a model call at :10/:40
# made ordinary generation stand down. :27/:57 starts early work 8 minutes
# before the next lease user (VIP at :35/:05) — longer than the lease TTL — so
# even a run whose model call hangs cannot block VIP/Premium, ordinary or
# European generation. If an ordinary run that started at :25/:55 is still
# going, the early run stands down and retries 30 minutes later.
27,57 * * * * /ops/cron-call.sh /api/admin/generate/early-run?limit=3
16,46 * * * * /ops/cron-call.sh /api/admin/generate/early-publish?limit=16
6,21,36,51 * * * * /ops/cron-call.sh /api/admin/generate/reassess?limit=3
